  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hfu - IMO TEST Biofouling</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The &#x201C;Accelerating Transfer of Environmentally sound Technologies through demonstration pilots to reduce biofouling and related emissions&#x201D; (TEST Biofouling). Project will assist developing countries to build their knowledge on control and management of biofouling and showcase effective approaches to biofouling management and the mitigation of environmental risks associated with the transfer of Invasive Aquatic Species (IAS) through biofouling by means of demonstration projects at both regional and country level. Invasive aquatic species (IAS) is a major threat to marine and coastal biodiversity. Improving biofouling management can also enhance ships&#x2019; energy efficiency and reduce greenhouse gas emissions from ships. The project also includes a Gender Action Plan with three key objectives: 1: Gender equality as a business case in the maritime sector. 2: Qualitative gender data gathered and analyzed. 3: Monitoring and delivery of IMO project-specific gender related activities.</narrative>
  </description>
